NAME
       setpgid, getpgid, setsid, getsid - process groups and sessions

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int   setpgid(pid_t pid, pid_t pgid);
       pid_t getpgid(pid_t pid);
       pid_t setsid(void);
       pid_t getsid(pid_t pid);

DESCRIPTION
       Process groups decide who receives a terminal signal. Ctrl-C
       sends SIGINT to the whole foreground group, so interrupting a
       script kills the command it is running as well as the script,
       rather than leaving one of them behind.

       A shell puts each pipeline in its own group and makes that group
       the foreground one; setsid starts a new session, which is what a
       daemon does to detach from the terminal.

RETURN VALUE
       0 or a pid on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ESRCH   no such process
       EPERM   the process is in another session

SEE ALSO
       kill(2), csh(1), openpty(2)
